<section class="content">

<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For preparing and leading the class. For catechist use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 70 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> The sacrament of Reconciliation as a living encounter with God's mercy: the Father's embrace of the son who returns.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that Christ himself, on the day of the Resurrection, gave the Church the power to forgive sins.</li>
<li>Know the various names of the sacrament and what each emphasizes.</li>
<li>Master the three acts of the penitent (contrition, confession, satisfaction) and absolution.</li>
<li>Overcome the fear, shame, and obstacles that prevent confession.</li>
<li>Learn the practical steps for making a good confession.</li>
<li>Connect the parable of the prodigal son with the sacrament.</li>
<li>Value frequent confession as a means of sanctification.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> "Receive the Holy Spirit. If you forgive the sins of any, they are forgiven; if you retain the sins of any, they are retained" (Jn 20:22-23)</p>
<p><strong>Catechism references:</strong> CCC 1420-1498</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Suggested Class Structure</h3>

<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.85rem;margin:16px 0">
<tr style="background:var(--gold-light)">
<th style="padding:8px;text-align:left;border:1px solid var(--border)">Section</th>
<th style="padding:8px;text-align:left;border:1px solid var(--border)">Duration</th>
<th style="padding:8px;text-align:left;border:1px solid var(--border)">What the catechist does</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">1. The Great Question: Rembrandt's embrace</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">10 min</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">Project or show an image of Rembrandt's <em>The Return of the Prodigal Son</em>. Narrate the parable (Lk 15:11-24). Ask: "Is there anything God cannot forgive? Is there something you believe is unforgivable?"</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">2. The names of the sacrament</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">5 min</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">List the five names. Each illuminates something distinct. Have the group repeat: it's not a courtroom; it's a feast.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">3. Christ institutes the sacrament</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">10 min</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">Read Jn 20:19-23 aloud. Emphasize: Easter evening, with the marks of the cross on the glorified body. Explain <em>in persona Christi</em>. Mention Mt 16:19 and the keys.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">4. The acts of the penitent</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">12 min</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">Contrition (perfect/imperfect; both valid). Confession (integral, in kind and number). Satisfaction (reparation, not punishment). Absolution: the moment God erases everything. Explain each with concrete examples.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">5. The seal of confession</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">5 min</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">Absolute, inviolable, without exceptions. Mention St. John Nepomucene. This is the information that most liberates those afraid to confess.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">6. Practical guide for confession</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">10 min</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">Walk through the ten practical steps. Teach the Act of Contrition. Explain examinations of conscience. If the group is small, you can do a mock confession (without confessing real sins, just the format).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">7. Scriptural Connection</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">5 min</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">Read Lk 15:20 (the father runs) and 2 Cor 5:18-20 (ministry of reconciliation). God runs; we run. We are ambassadors of reconciliation.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">8. For Reflection</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">8 min</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">Choose two questions. Pair work. Only share with the whole group if someone wants to. Never force sharing personal experiences of sin.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">9. Closing: Key Idea + Prayer</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">5 min</td>
<td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--border)">Read the Key Idea. Pray the workbook prayer. Hand out the workbook. Remind them of the parish confession times. If possible, offer confessions at the end of class or at the next session.</td>
</tr>
</table>

